Let a tablet install an extension at all.

A tablet or a 2in1 got the mobile store, whose button is "add to home
screen" -- so an extension could not be installed at all, which is the
whole point of having the store.

The store reads the User-Agent string and nothing else. Four shapes were
compared on a tablet-sized window with the devtools protocol setting the UA
and the Client Hints together:

  PC; OpenHarmony 7.0; Android 10   mobile site, "add to home screen"
  PC; OpenHarmony 7.0               mobile site
  ... with UA-CH platform Linux     mobile site, so the hints are ignored
  PC; OpenHarmony 7.0; X11          desktop site, install button

One windowing token is the difference. It cannot go in the UA everyone
gets: with "X11; Linux" in it, qq.com serves its phone pages. So the store
gets it on the navigation, through the same per-entry override "desktop
site" uses, and every other site is untouched. Phones are left alone
entirely -- they have no extensions UI, and the desktop store would be
unusable on one.

The Client Hints stay as they are. The string still names OpenHarmony, so
platform HarmonyOS agrees with it; a UA-CH platform disagreeing with the UA
is exactly what read as a spoofed browser when this port last tried it.

Second, the update query said os=HarmonyOS. That string picks the package
the server sends, and there is no such platform there, so it answered
nothing: every CRX download and every extension update asked for a platform
that does not exist. It says linux now, which with the arm64 already beside
it is a combination the server serves, and an extension's CRX is the same
bytes on all of them.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after ohos-ua-chrome-android.patch.

diff --git a/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.h b/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.h
--- a/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.h
+++ b/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.h
@@ -40,6 +40,13 @@
 // presentation without restarting Chromium.
 std::string GetUserAgentForOhos(bool mobile);
 blink::UserAgentMetadata GetUserAgentMetadataForOhos(bool mobile);
+
+// The desktop HarmonyOS UA with an X11 token in its platform section, for
+// the Chrome Web Store and nothing else. See
+// chrome/browser/ui/ohos/shell_store_user_agent_ohos.h for why one token
+// decides whether extensions can be installed at all, and why it cannot go
+// in the UA everyone gets.
+std::string GetOhosStoreUserAgent();
 #endif
 
 // Return UserAgentMetadata, `only_low_entropy_ch` indicates whether only
diff --git a/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc b/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc
--- a/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc
+++ b/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc
@@ -610,6 +610,24 @@
   metadata.form_factors = GetFormFactorsClientHint(metadata, mobile);
   return metadata;
 }
+
+std::string GetOhosStoreUserAgent() {
+  // The desktop string with X11 added to the platform section, so
+  // "Mozilla/5.0 (Tablet; OpenHarmony 7.0)" becomes
+  // "Mozilla/5.0 (Tablet; OpenHarmony 7.0; X11)".
+  //
+  // Written as an insertion rather than a fourth branch of
+  // BuildOhosUserAgent() so that --user-agent, which replaces the whole
+  // string, still gets the token in the right place.
+  std::string user_agent = GetUserAgentForOhos(/*mobile=*/false);
+  const size_t platform_end = user_agent.find(')');
+  if (platform_end == std::string::npos) {
+    return user_agent;
+  }
+  return base::StrCat({std::string_view(user_agent).substr(0, platform_end),
+                       "; X11",
+                       std::string_view(user_agent).substr(platform_end)});
+}
 #endif
 
